# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 1: calls WU (cycle s1) / calls BRG (cycle s3)

== a test at school tomorrow
tier: everyday
at: school
stages: child
age: 6-14
calls: WU
tone: trouble
life: school
horizon: moment
roles: parent, grandparent, friend, a teacher
earth: a spelling or maths test tomorrow, and the worksheet is still blank
times: Nearly every school child, many times a year, from weekly spelling tests to end-of-term papers (estimate)
gap: 0-.4
scene: Tomorrow there is a test, and {N} has a page of sums that will not stay put in their head.
scene W: The teacher said everyone must be ready tomorrow. {N} wants to be one of the ones who is.
scene U: {N} spreads the worksheets across the bed. Somewhere in them is a pattern, if only it would show itself.
scene B: Whoever scores best tomorrow gets to sit by the window for a month. {N} wants that seat.
scene R: The sun is out, {friend} is calling from the street, and the test is not until tomorrow.
scene G: {parent} sat the same test in the same school at the same age. The old exercise book is still on the shelf.
- W | revise the way the teacher showed you, then go to bed on time | habit | v: conformity | chance: 75
- U | make flashcards and test yourself until you get every one | habit | v: achievement, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | chance: 82
- B | get the answers from an older kid who sat the same test | v: achievement | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: cheating; backfire: caught, a zero and a note home | chance: 60
- R | turn the hard sums into a rhyme, and chant it until it sticks | v: hedonism, stimulation | chance: 65
- G | ask a grandparent to help you revise, the way they once helped your parent | v: tradition, benevolence | act: ask a grandparent to help them revise, the way that grandparent once helped their parent | chance: 75
- W>U | stay after class and ask the teacher to explain what you missed | v: self-direction, conformity | chance: 75
- U>B | work out which questions are worth the most marks and learn only those | v: achievement | chance: 60
- B>R | pretend to be sick so you can stay home tomorrow | v: hedonism | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: lying; backfire: found out, and the test the day after anyway | chance: 65
- R>G | cry that you cannot do it, and let mum or dad hold you | v: security, benevolence | act: cry that they cannot do it, and let mum or dad hold them | chance: 75
- G>W | revise at the kitchen table while the family keeps you company | habit | v: conformity, tradition | chance: 78
works: The questions are the very ones {N} prepared for.
works: The test comes back with a smile drawn at the top.
fails: Half the page stays blank.
fails: The mark comes home, and so does a note.

== a stray dog follows you home
tier: everyday
stages: child
age: 4-14
calls: BRG
tone: mixed
life: home, nature
horizon: week
roles: parent, sibling, a neighbour
earth: a thin dog with a collar and no tag follows you from the park
times: About 1 in 4 children, once or twice in childhood; about 3 million dogs enter US shelters a year, many of them found loose (ASPCA) (estimate)
gap: 4-8
share: .25
rate: 1
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
scene: A thin brown dog has followed {N} all the way from the park and now sits at the gate, wagging.
scene W: The dog has a collar but no tag. Somewhere, someone must be missing it, and {N} feels that is now their problem.
scene U: The dog follows {N} home, and {N} cannot stop wondering where it came from and why it chose them.
scene B: A dog follows {N} home. {N} has always wanted one, and {parent} has always said no. Nobody has to know.
scene R: A scruffy dog trots after {N} all the way home, and {N} is already in love.
scene G: A stray dog curls up by {Ns} back door as if it has always lived there.
- W | take it to the vet so they can find its owner | v: benevolence, conformity | mark: helped someone in need | chance: 70
- U | work out where it came from by asking up and down the street | v: self-direction | chance: 70
- B | hide it in the shed and keep it for yourself | v: hedonism, power | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: not yours, and no pets allowed; backfire: found, a row at home | chance: 60
- R | run inside shouting that you have a dog now | v: stimulation, hedonism | chance: 55
- G | feed it and let it decide whether to stay | v: universalism (nature) | chance: 60
- W>R | promise to walk it every single day if you can keep it | binds | v: benevolence, hedonism | act: promise to walk it every single day if they can keep it | chance: 45
- U>G | find out what it needs and make it a warm box with water | v: universalism (nature), benevolence | chance: 85
- B>W | find the owner yourself, door to door, and ask if there is a reward | v: achievement, power | mark: helped someone in need | chance: 55
- R>U | follow the dog back the way it came, to see where it lives | v: stimulation, self-direction | mark: took a wild risk | closed: approval: wandering off alone; backfire: lost, and a search party | chance: 55
- G>B | keep it in the garden, where it scares off the kids who bother you | v: power, security | closed: approval: keeping a lost dog to frighten other children; backfire: the dog snaps at a child, and the owner comes for it | act: keep it in the garden, where it scares off the kids who bother them | chance: 45
works: The dog ends up where it belongs, and {N} goes to bed happy.
works: {parent} sighs, and says the dog can stay a while.
fails: The dog runs off in the night and does not come back.
fails: There is a row at home about the dog, and {N} loses the argument.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: starting school (pairs D1a)

== starting school
tier: life event
at: school
stages: child
age: 4-7
per_year: .35 0 0 0 0 0
drivers: prosper+.1 unrest-.3
times: once, between four and seven
likelier: a country with school from an early age, peace
rarer: war, displacement, a family that keeps children home
tone: mixed
life: school
horizon: years
roles: parent, sibling, a teacher, the other children
earth: your first day at school
scene: It is {Ns} first day at school. The building is huge, and full of strangers.
scene W: {N} has a new bag, new shoes, and a list of rules {parent} went over at breakfast.
scene U: {N} walks into a classroom full of books, maps and jars, and wants to know what all of it is for.
scene B: There are thirty children in the class and one teacher. {N} already sees who the others listen to.
scene R: The school gate swings open, and the noise from the playground hits {N} like a wave.
scene G: {sibling} went to this school, and {parent} before that. {N} walks in holding a hand.
- W | line up, listen, and learn the rules quickly | habit | v: conformity | chance: 85
- U | ask the teacher a hundred questions on the first day | door | v: self-direction | chance: 80
- B | make friends with the kid the others already listen to | v: power, security | mark: made a friend | tags: win:ties+.05 | chance: 75
- R | run straight into the playground and join the first game you see | v: stimulation | tags: win:ties+.05 | chance: 90
- G | stay close to your sibling and the kids from your street | v: security, tradition | chance: 75
- WU | sit at the front and do exactly what is asked, and do it well | habit | v: achievement, conformity | chance: 82
- BR | push to the front of every line and grab the best seat | v: power, hedonism | closed: approval: pushing; backfire: told off in front of everyone | chance: 75
- UG | spend every break watching the ants by the fence | v: universalism (nature), self-direction | chance: 60
- WR | volunteer for every job, brave and eager to help | v: benevolence, stimulation | chance: 80
- BG | keep to your own little gang and guard your corner of the yard | v: security, power | chance: 75
works: By the end of the week {N} has a friend and a favourite peg for their coat.
works: {N} comes home every day full of stories.
fails: {N} cries every morning at the gate for weeks.
fails: School starts badly, and {N} dreads Mondays for a long time.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 2: calls UB (cycle s2) / calls WRG (cycle s4)

== a game of hide and seek
tier: everyday
stages: child
age: 4-11
calls: UB
tone: joy
life: play, friends
horizon: moment
roles: friend, sibling, the kids on the street
earth: hide and seek with the kids on your street, as the light goes
times: Nearly every child, many times a year, most of all on long summer evenings (estimate)
gap: 0-.5
scene: {friend} is counting to fifty against the garage door, and the whole street, gardens and hedges and bins, is a hiding place.
scene W: Everyone agreed the rules: no hiding indoors, no moving once hidden. {N} means to keep to them, even if the others do not.
scene U: {N} has watched three rounds already and knows exactly where {friend} looks first, and where {friend} never looks at all.
scene B: Last one found wins, and the winner picks the next game. {N} wants to pick the next game.
scene R: Forty-one, forty-two. {Ns} heart is hammering, there is no time to think, only to run.
scene G: {N} folds into the long grass behind the shed, among the snails and the beetles, and goes very still.
- W | call foul when the seeker peeks, and make them count again from one | v: conformity | chance: 45
- U | study where the seeker always looks first, and hide in the one place they never check | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 65
- B | sneak indoors, which is against the rules, where nobody will ever look | v: power, achievement | chance: 85
- R | burst out of the hedge and race for home before the seeker can turn round | body: light | v: stimulation | chance: 60
- G | curl up in the long grass and keep so still a robin lands beside you | v: universalism (nature) | act: curl up in the long grass and keep so still a robin lands beside them | chance: 50
- W>B | make a new rule that the littlest kids always have to be the seeker | v: power | closed: approval: an unfair rule; backfire: the little ones go home crying, and the big ones get the blame | chance: 55
- U>R | leave your coat poking out of one bush as a decoy, and hide in another | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 60
- B>G | let one of the little ones share your secret spot, if they swear to stay quiet | v: benevolence, power | chance: 45
- R>W | jump out on purpose, so the little one who keeps losing finally finds someone | v: benevolence | chance: 92
- G>U | stay hidden long after the game ends, learning the sounds of the street at dusk | v: self-direction, universalism (nature) | closed: approval: staying out after dark when the others have gone home; backfire: a worried parent calling up and down the street | chance: 75
works: {N} is the last one found, and gets to choose the next game.
works: Nobody finds {N} until the streetlights come on, and everyone agrees it was the best round ever.
fails: {N} is found in the first ten seconds, giggling.
fails: A row breaks out over the rules, and the game ends early.

== your little cousin comes to stay
tier: everyday
stages: child
age: 5-12
calls: WRG
tone: mixed
life: family
horizon: week
roles: a younger cousin, parent, grandparent
earth: your little cousin stays for a week and sleeps on a mattress in your room
