gap: 2-4
share: .5
rate: 1
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
scene: {Ns} little cousin arrives with a rucksack nearly as big as they are, and will sleep on a mattress in {Ns} room for a whole week.
scene W: {parent} says {N} is the host now, and a good host shares. {N} takes that very seriously.
scene U: The little cousin talks with a funny accent, believes in strange things and knows a card game {N} has never heard of.
scene B: The little cousin gets the attention, the bigger slice and the front seat. {N} is counting every one.
scene R: A whole week with someone to run, shout and build dens with, and {N} can hardly wait for the car to pull up.
scene G: The little cousin has {Ns} grandparent's chin and {Ns} parent's laugh. Family is family, even the small loud ones.
- W | give your cousin your own bed and take the mattress, because guests come first | v: benevolence, conformity | chance: 80
- U | learn your cousin's card game, then win every round by secretly marking the cards | v: achievement | closed: approval: cheating; backfire: caught, and the cousin tells the whole family | chance: 75
- B | charge your cousin a sweet for every go on your bike | v: power | chance: 70
- R | whisper and giggle under the covers long after lights out | v: hedonism, stimulation | closed: approval: lights out means lights out; backfire: told off, and moved to separate rooms | chance: 90
- G | take your cousin to the den by the stream that only family knows about | v: tradition, benevolence | tags: win:ties+.05 | chance: 78
- W>G | make up your cousin's bed properly and set out a welcome card from the whole family | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 90
- U>W | explain the house rules to your cousin, with a list, so they stay out of trouble | v: conformity, benevolence | chance: 55
- B>U | swap your cousin your worst toy for their book of magic tricks | door | v: self-direction, power | chance: 63
- R>B | challenge your cousin to a race to the car, winner gets the front seat | v: achievement, stimulation | chance: 50
- G>R | roughhouse with your cousin on the lawn like a pair of puppies | body: light | v: hedonism, stimulation | chance: 75
works: By the end of the week the two of them are inseparable, and both cry when the car comes.
works: The little cousin goes home with a drawing of {N} and a new favourite game.
fails: The cousin cries for home every night, and somehow {N} gets the blame.
fails: By Wednesday they are fighting over everything, and {parent} has to step in.

