scene W: {N} has had two slices already and {sibling} has had one, and {N} knows exactly what fair looks like, even when it hurts.
scene U: {N} squints at the slice. There must be a cleverer way to settle this than shouting.
scene B: One slice, and the first one to the plate gets it. {N} is two steps closer.
scene R: The smell of chocolate fills the whole kitchen, and {N} wants that slice more than anything in the world.
scene G: {grandparent} baked the cake the way it has been baked for every birthday in the family, and there is one slice left.
- W | cut it exactly in half: one of you cuts, the other chooses | v: universalism (fairness), conformity | act: cut it exactly in half, one cutting and the other choosing | chance: 88
- U | challenge your sibling to a times-table quiz, winner takes the slice | v: achievement | chance: 45
- B | lick the top of it, so nobody else will want it | v: power, hedonism | chance: 90
- R | grab it and stuff it in before anyone can say a word | body: light | v: hedonism | chance: 80
- G | leave it for your grandparent, who baked it and has not had a bite | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 70
- W>R | hold a fair contest for it: the funniest joke wins, and everyone votes | v: hedonism, universalism (fairness) | chance: 70
- U>G | cut it into tiny squares so everyone in the family gets a taste | v: benevolence | chance: 92
- B>W | give your sibling the slice, on a promise that you get the next one | v: power, universalism (fairness) | chance: 90
- R>U | beg to bake a whole new cake right now, so you learn how it is done | door | v: self-direction, stimulation | mark: learned a skill | chance: 45
- G>B | claim it by family custom: the birthday child always gets the last slice | v: tradition, power | chance: 55
works: The last slice is settled, and nobody ends up in tears.
works: Everyone laughs, and the plate is licked clean.
fails: The slice ends up face down on the floor, and nobody gets it.
fails: {sibling} storms off, and {N} is sent upstairs.

