scene R: The sea is freezing and enormous, and {N} is already running at it, shrieking.
scene G: {N} digs both feet into the cool wet sand and watches the waves come and go, come and go.
- W | stay between the flags and keep an eye on the younger ones in the water | v: security, benevolence | chance: 90
- U | spend the day in the rock pools, finding out the name of every creature | v: self-direction | mark: learned a skill | chance: 90
- B | dig a moat round your family's spot and charge the other kids a shell to cross | v: power | chance: 75
- R | run into the waves again and again, until your lips go purple | body: light | v: stimulation, hedonism | chance: 90
- G | lie buried to the neck in warm sand, listening to the sea | v: hedonism, universalism (nature) | chance: 95
- W>G | pick up every bit of litter on the beach, for the gulls and the fish | v: universalism (nature) | chance: 80
- U>W | read the tide board and warn your family before the water reaches the towels | v: security, benevolence | chance: 75
- B>U | trade your spade for a boy's snorkel mask so you can see under the water | door | v: self-direction | chance: 55
- R>B | race your sibling to the rocks and back; the loser buys the ice creams | body: light | v: achievement, stimulation | chance: 50
- G>R | wander off along the shore after the crabs, further than ever before | door | v: stimulation, universalism (nature) | mark: took a wild risk | closed: approval: wandering out of sight; backfire: a frightened search and a cross parent | chance: 70
works: {N} comes home sunburnt, salty and happier than in weeks.
works: The day ends with chips on the sea wall and a sky full of gulls.
fails: A wasp sting, a lost spade and a long sulk in the car.
fails: The weather turns, and everyone runs for the car in the rain.

