scene B: Empty houses have things left in them, and nobody around to say whose they are.
scene R: The gate creaks, the wind moans in the chimney, and {Ns} heart is going like a drum. It is the best feeling in the world.
scene G: Ivy has grown over the windows, and a fox has made its den under the porch. The house is going back to the wild.
