- R>B | wail until your parents give in and let you sleep in their bed | habit | v: hedonism, security | act: wail until their parents give in and let them sleep in their bed | chance: 75
- G>R | slip out to the back step to feel the warm rain on your face | body: light | v: stimulation, universalism (nature) | mark: defied an authority | closed: approval: out of bed in a storm; backfire: caught, soaked and scolded | chance: 70
