# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: the family moves to a new town (triads from D2a)

== the family moves to a new town
tier: life event
stages: child juvenile
age: 12-17
per_year: .03 .03 0 0 0 0
drivers: prosper+.3 community-.3 ties-.2 era+.2
gap: 2-4
times: about 10 in 100 children and 7 in 100 teenagers a year move home with their family, and about four in ten of those moves go to another town (D37, data and estimate); US moves are at a record low, about half the rate of the 1960s
likelier: a parent's new job, a split, renting, a growing economy, cheap and easy travel
rarer: owning the home, grandparents and family nearby, a close community, a family farm or business
moves: yes
tone: mixed
life: home, friends
horizon: years
roles: parent, sibling, friend, grandparent
earth: the family moves to a town you have only seen on a map
scene: The house is full of boxes and the walls are bare. Tomorrow the van leaves for a town {N} has only ever seen on a map, and all of {Ns} friends are staying here.
scene W: {N} has a list of everyone to keep in touch with, and means to keep at it, not just for the first month.
scene U: {N} has looked the new town up: its river, its schools, the late bus to the city. It might be interesting.
scene B: In the new town nobody knows who {N} was. {N} can be anyone at all.
scene R: Nobody asked {N}. {N} is leaving friends, a team and a whole life behind, and is furious about it.
scene G: {N} walks past the old school, the park and the corner shop one last time, trying to fix each one in memory.
- W | promise every friend you will keep in touch, and message them every week | v: benevolence | tags: win:ties+.05 | tech: phone | chance: 55
- U | look up everything about the new town: the schools, the clubs, the buses | v: self-direction | chance: 70
- B | decide to reinvent yourself at the new school, as someone people look up to | identity | v: power, self-direction | chance: 55
- R | throw a loud goodbye party for your friends on the last night | v: hedonism, benevolence | chance: 75
- G | walk your old streets one last time, and promise yourself you will come back | binds | v: tradition | chance: 65
- WUR | join a team or a club in the first week, to find your feet fast | door | v: self-direction, stimulation | chance: 78
- WUG | set up your new room with all your old things, just as it was | v: security, tradition | chance: 70
- WBG | stay close to your family and keep a low profile until you know who to trust | v: security | chance: 55
- UBR | work out who runs things at the new school, and get on their side fast | v: power, security | chance: 65
- BRG | square up to the first kid at the new school who tries to push you around | body: light | v: power | closed: approval: fighting; backfire: suspended in the first week, with a reputation | act: square up to the first kid at the new school who tries to push them around | role: men | chance: 60
works: Within a month {N} has a new best friend and a favourite path to school.
works: The new town has a river, a library and a kid next door who is just as new.
fails: {N} spends lunchtimes alone for weeks, and the old friends slowly stop replying.
fails: {N} begs every night to go back, and nothing feels right for a long time.

